Title: OCTOBER
Credit: written by
Author: a Python script
Source: inspired by the FOX promo that said it couldn't be done (https://vimeo.com/45736773)
Draft date: October 21, 2026
Notes: The 2004 World Series. Unofficial. Not affiliated with FOX or MLB.


FADE IN:

INT. A LIVING ROOM - OCTOBER 2006 - NIGHT

A TV glows. Between innings, a FOX playoff promo: a typewriter pecks out a play-by-play over the action. "Percival delivers a 98 mph fastball to Bonds. Bonds lifts it to center. It should be caught fo--" The real ball keeps going, and the typed line gets crossed out mid-word.

PROMO ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
You can't script October.

PATRUCK, on the couch, takes a chip. Chews. Doesn't argue. Lets FOX have it.

INT. GROUP CHAT - OCTOBER 2026 - NIGHT

20 years later. Little gray dots pulse.

THE BELIEVER
Remember that FOX promo? "You can't script October"?

PATRUCK
Classic.

THE BELIEVER
20 years, and you never once pushed back on that.

PATRUCK
...Was I supposed to?

THE BELIEVER
Pick a year.

PATRUCK
2004.

INT. A TYPEWRITER - CONTINUOUS

Keys clack. A page fills up before anyone has thrown a pitch.

THE SCRIPT
(typing)
The 2004 World Series. The Boston Red Sox beat the St. Louis Cardinals, 4-0. It ends in Game 4, on a Wednesday.

PATRUCK
(mouth full)
Huh.

THE SCRIPT
(typing)
A sweep only goes one way. Four straight. Picking the right team was the hard part.

EXT. THE BALLPARK - WEDNESDAY, OCTOBER 27, 2004 - NIGHT

World Series, Game 4. The stands are a wall of noise. A full moon hangs over the upper deck, right where the math put it.

INT. FOX BROADCAST BOOTH - CONTINUOUS

THE PLAY-BY-PLAY ANNOUNCER and THE COLOR ANALYST lean into their microphones. A FOX graphic reads WORLD SERIES.

PLAY-BY-PLAY ANNOUNCER
The Boston Red Sox are one out away.

COLOR ANALYST
A sweep. Four games. That's not a script, that's a pamphlet.

COLOR ANALYST
Eighty-six years. Over.

COLOR ANALYST
And look up. That's a total lunar eclipse.

PLAY-BY-PLAY ANNOUNCER
(rising)
And the Boston Red Sox are World Series champions!

INT. A LIVING ROOM - CONTINUOUS

PATRUCK stares at the TV, then at the typed page in THE BELIEVER's hand. Every line matches. Nothing is crossed out.

PATRUCK
Not one line crossed out?

THE BELIEVER
Not one.

INT. A LIVING ROOM - OCTOBER 2006 - NIGHT

Back on the old TV, the same promo plays again. The typewriter. The crossed-out line.

PROMO ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
You can't script October.

THE SCRIPT
(typing)
I just did.

For the first time in 20 years, PATRUCK sets down the chip and looks the TV in the eye.

PATRUCK
(finally)
Yeah, you CAN script October.

> FADE OUT.

> THE END <
